{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1341921-the-\u00e6on-\u00e6xpansion-\u00e6xpanded-my-understanding-of-the-setting","id":1341921,"title":"The \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion \u00c6xpanded my understanding of the setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-17T12:38:48-07:00","id":1341921,"title":"The \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion \u00c6xpanded my understanding of the setting","content":"First and foremost, if you aren't a backer and haven't seen it yet, get hyped for the \u00c6xpansion because it is fantastic.<br /> <br /> The one thing that specifically brings me here are the Psiad Rules, not anything specific about them, but how they grow and evolve the setting, and the setting history. What Psiads can do in Aberrant are different than what Psiads can do in \u00c6on and my mind is blown, especially in how this applies to \u00c6on era Aberrants (henceforth referred to as \u00c6bberants). I was initially somewhat perturbed by the fact that the Aberrant rules for Novas didn't let you emulate what \u00c6berrants do, specifically make Sub-Aberrant Mutants, but then I realized if Psiads can change in the 100+ years between Aberrant and \u00c6on, so can Novas. Any difference between \u00c6berrants and Novas can be explained by the evolution/degeneration of the Aberrant condition. Although how much of that is a change in humans themselves or a change in the Quantum/Psi fields of the continuum is up for debate. Psiad's increased ability to wield QK powers could potentially be directly tied to the increased flux generation and power sharing of the \u00c6berrants.<br /> <br /> Edit: for the sake of conversation with folks that don't have access to the book, Psiads get increased access to Quantakinesis in \u00c6on than they do in Aberrant due to Psiads going through a sort of evolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 10-17-2019, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T13:56:13-07:00","id":1341938,"title":"","content":"I share your view of the book And how it give new ways to view the setting. Not only that, but also the way humans learned to control Nova Eruptions and how it would evolve to world to a very different setting if give enough time, with the natural evolutions (Novas and Psiads) being gradually replaced by engineered ones (Superiors and Psions).<br /> <br /> There are a few powers in 1e that work on the way the Novas evolved to the Aberrants in Aeon, like the power Sin-Eater and Geryon, and how they deal with Transformations (formerly Aberrations). We will see some about it in the future for sure...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T14:10:03-07:00","id":1341941,"title":"","content":"I agree. Completely. In fact, as I said elsewhere, the fact that sapients can manipulate the Psi and Quantum (and Flux) templates to me is a very interesting element of the Trinity Continuum. The idea that a race could be like &quot;We like the idea but...&quot; and then create a variant that is constrained in some ways or loose in others would be really cool. <br /> <br /> One of the random ideas that I had was a Nova-variant that basically restricted Quantum Powers along particular broad categories rather than making them an 'anything goes' sort of way. <br /> <br /> But yeah Aeon Aexpansion is super favorite book of mine. The Psiad and Superior rules are marvelous. (So is everything else but those rules stand out as spectacular to me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T19:42:43-07:00","id":1341996,"title":"","content":"A little detail I was thinking.<br /> <br /> The 2104 event allowed Psiads to learn QK, that\u2019s great, but N-Day event maybe caused a similar effect, where humans were all limited to a lower level quantum manipulation. Maybe, just maybe, Mal did more than just allowing Novas to erupt, maybe he allowed them to reach a level or a set of powers that was impossible before, even for him.<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe N-Day allowed Novas to have powers that goes beyond their body, before that all novas (or Proto-novas) were limited to powers that affect only their body and senses, like Superiors. Even Mal was limited (like Burano was), for example, before that he was unable to control plasma or any kind of energy: than the N-Day event unlocked that on all the pre N-Day novas.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, before N-Day it was impossible to gather Flux and Transcendence, as oppose of later.<br /> <br /> that is just a speculation, but it hit me really hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T20:05:13-07:00","id":1341998,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea that the N-Day Eruption boosted what a Nova could achieve. Maybe before hand Quantum was limited to say 5 and what powers could be achieved were also limited. But afterward the sky was the limit, and so was Flux. On a metagame level maybe Experience costs were higher, so it took more time and effort to advance. <br /> <br /> All this would help explain those who were Novas pre-N-Day. They seemed to have been lower level people and then upon the moment they gain boosts in powers. <br /> <br /> It could also help to explain how particular moments in the Continuum lead to variant versions - the starting events led to slight modifications to what can be expressed. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> As another note Aeon Aexpansion had me thinking on what the potential endgame for Psi users are. Like humanity is special in its access to QK, what other specials could occur in time. What would humanity in a few thousand years be like, no just in Psi but also Quantum. Its marvelous to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}